# Phase 0. Install with: crontab -e — adjust paths.
#
# ON macOS, USE scripts/launchd/ INSTEAD. cron is subject to TCC there and
# fails completely silently without Full Disk Access — a correct crontab line
# installed on 2026-08-24 (macOS 26.5) never executed once, with no error
# anywhere. This file is kept for portability to other hosts.
#
# Timing note (measured 2026-08-24): two consecutive sweeps walked 1,319 and
# 1,320 pages of the open universe in 412s and 427s — ~7 minutes, roughly half
# the 15-minute interval. The universe nearly doubled in the preceding 15 hours
# (698,892 -> 1,319,432 markets, essentially all MVE combos), so this margin is
# not guaranteed; watch capture.log if sweeps approach 15 minutes.
# capture.py takes a lock in data/kalshi_quant/; if a sweep overruns, the next
# tick exits immediately rather than doubling the request rate into Kalshi's
# limiter. Overruns therefore degrade to a 30-minute cadence on their own.
#
# settle() is driven by our own snapshots, not by the global settled feed, so it
# is cheap: measured 2026-08-24, 2,750 resolutions over 145 requests in 35s, and
# 10s when little is pending. It is idempotent — the work list is "captured,
# closed, not yet resolved" — so a missed run costs nothing and a gap of any
# length repairs itself rather than falling outside a fixed window.
#
# It runs at :12, inside the gap between snapshot sweeps. Snapshots start on the
# quarter hour and have taken up to 585s, so they occupy roughly :00-:10,
# :15-:25, :30-:40, :45-:55. The two jobs take separate locks and would not
# block each other, but keeping them disjoint avoids doubling the request rate
# into Kalshi's limiter.
#
# cron runs with a minimal PATH and no shell profile, so `uv` is called by
# absolute path. Find yours with: command -v uv

*/15 * * * * cd /Users/hermesagent/development/avo-forecast && /Users/hermesagent/miniconda3/bin/uv run python -m experiments.kalshi_quant.capture snapshot >> data/capture.log 2>&1
12   * * * * cd /Users/hermesagent/development/avo-forecast && /Users/hermesagent/miniconda3/bin/uv run python -m experiments.kalshi_quant.capture settle   >> data/capture.log 2>&1
